          1.05
        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Cada isla tenía un lugar de salto, una roca alta sobre el mar. Se llamaba leina.",
          "en": "Every island had a leaping place, a high rock above the sea. It was called a leina."
        },
        {
          "es": "El más famoso era Kaʻena, la punta más al oeste de Oʻahu.",
          "en": "The most famous was Kaʻena Point, the far western tip of Oʻahu."
        },
        {
          "es": "Allí las almas se paraban en las rocas, miraban el agua oscura, y saltaban.",
          "en": "There the souls stood on the rocks, looked down at the dark water, and jumped."
        },
        {
          "es": "Pero no todas las almas encontraban el camino. Algunas se perdían, y vagaban de noche por la tierra.",
          "en": "But not every soul found its way. Some got lost, and wandered the land at night."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los espíritus de la familia, los ʻaumakua, podían encontrarlas y guiarlas. A veces, hasta devolvían un alma a su cuerpo.",
          "en": "The family spirits, the ʻaumakua, could find them and guide them. Sometimes, they even sent a soul back to its body."
        }
      ],
